{"id":"000VJ9","title":"Controlled chaos","author":"Artham","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-21T18:43:13+00:00","posted":"Heute, 16:00 Uhr","rules":"The first chaos construction I made. I was quite worried but it turned out not that bad in the end :) I hope you enjoy solving it.\n\nClick here to solve on Sudokupad\n\nFill the grid with digits from 1 to 8 so that no digit repeats in a row or column.\n\nWithin each outlined 4x4 square, starting from the circle, color a connected group of cells using only orthogonal moves. The resulting shape must not branch or touch itself.\n\nThe path and the leftover cells in the square form two separate regions in which every digit from 1 to 8 appears exactly once. The leftover cells are not necessarily all connected.\n\nNumbers outside the grid indicate the sum of all cells seen in that direction until hitting the first region boundary.\n\nDigit in the circle must appear in one of the adjacent squares.","solutionCode":"Last row from left to right","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/qr4brhnbfy","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/qr4brhnbfy","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":8,"cols":8,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-21T18:43:13+00:00"}